    {
      "id": "CTI-02",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-compact-type-compression",
      "title": "Compression to the lowest compact type is a weighted compact average",
      "statement": "If all opposite-sign parameter gaps are at least h≥120 m q^(3/2), q=min(p,s), then for a highest-weight unit w in the lowest type S, u,v∈S and Hermitian X anticommuting with the signature matrix, ⟨v,π(exp X)u⟩=dim(S)∫_K Φ(k⁻¹ exp(X) k)⟨v,π(k)w⟩⟨π(k)w,u⟩ dk with Haar probability on K.",
      "hypotheses": "The signed coordinates retain the strictly decreasing Harish-Chandra order, and λ_a−(m−1)/2 is integral. Negative powers in the scalar product are evaluated at positive leading principal minors on every real ray. The projection used in the identity is the orthogonal projection to the lowest K-type in π.",
      "dependencies": [
        "CTI-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "normalization-compact-type-integral"
      ],
